1. FlyWire connectome data: CC BY-NC 4.0 (NOT under the MIT License; non-commercial use only)
=====================================================================================================

Files:
  koz/brains/flybrain/original/brain/locomotion/neurons.json
  koz/brains/flybrain/original/brain/locomotion/positions.csv
  koz/brains/flybrain/original/brain/locomotion/weights.npz

These files are derived from the FlyWire connectome, materialization v783, which is published under
the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/). These derived files are shared under the same
licence: you may copy and adapt them with credit, for non-commercial purposes only.

Credit:
  Dorkenwald, S. et al. "Neuronal wiring diagram of an adult brain." Nature 634, 124-138 (2024).
  Schlegel, P. et al. "Whole-brain annotation and multi-connectome cell typing of Drosophila."
  Nature 634, 139-152 (2024).
  FlyWire (https://flywire.ai), Princeton University and the FlyWire Consortium.

Changes made in Islombek Turdiyev's robot-car project: a 2,282-neuron circuit for locomotion and looming was selected;
its neuron IDs, 2-D positions and cell types (neurons.json, positions.csv) and its synapse counts,
signed by neurotransmitter (weights.npz), were saved for a real-time simulation. Nothing was trained.

